// Pull request author: frack113
// Change: update to existing rule
// Title: Suspicious Ping/Del Command Combination
// Sigma ID: 5c75dfce-62f6-4d96-95dc-fb09a2ae7022
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Ilya Krestinichev
// Date: 2022-11-03 | Modified: 2026-11-06
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1070.004
// Description: Detects a method often used by ransomware. Which combines the "ping" to wait a couple of seconds
//   and then "del" to delete the file in question. Its used to hide the file responsible for the
//   initial infection for example
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://blog.sygnia.co/kaseya-ransomware-supply-chain-attack
//   - https://media.kasperskycontenthub.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/43/2022/06/23093553/Common-TTPs-of-the-modern-ransomware_low-res.pdf
//   - https://www.acronis.com/en-us/blog/posts/lockbit-ransomware/
//   - https://symantec-enterprise-blogs.security.com/blogs/threat-intelligence/blackbyte-exbyte-ransomware
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/7490edb4783550895f8ac7b1ff297eaa8fda0d2a/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_cmd_ping_del_combined_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains " -n " or ProcessCommandLine contains " /n " or ProcessCommandLine contains " –n " or ProcessCommandLine contains " —n " or ProcessCommandLine contains " ―n ") and ProcessCommandLine contains "Nul" and (ProcessCommandLine contains " -f " or ProcessCommandLine contains " /f " or ProcessCommandLine contains " –f " or ProcessCommandLine contains " —f " or ProcessCommandLine contains " ―f " or ProcessCommandLine contains " -q " or ProcessCommandLine contains " /q " or ProcessCommandLine contains " –q " or ProcessCommandLine contains " —q " or ProcessCommandLine contains " ―q ") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "ping" and ProcessCommandLine contains "del ")
